+ between different known types errors at run time
(diag.mixed_type_operator, warning, on the +): string + number, number +
date (the reverse of the supported date + number), a product added to a
string (precedence honored), and a chain that reports once on the + that
introduces the mismatch.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Caption;
	:PARAMETERS nCount, dWhen, oRec;
	:DECLARE sCaption, dLater;
	sCaption := "Total: " + 5;
	sCaption := sCaption + nCount;
	dLater := 7 + dWhen;
	sCaption := nCount * 2 + sCaption;
	sCaption := oRec:Name + " - " + nCount + " items";
	:RETURN sCaption + LimsString(dLater);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Caption;
	:PARAMETERS nCount, dWhen, oRec;
	:DECLARE sCaption, dLater;
	sCaption := "Total: " + 5;
	sCaption := sCaption + nCount;
	dLater := 7 + dWhen;
	sCaption := nCount * 2 + sCaption;
	sCaption := oRec:Name + " - " + nCount + " items";
	:RETURN sCaption + LimsString(dLater);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:24-4:25 warning mixed_type_operator: Mixed types in '+' operation: string + numeric. The '+' operator requires both operands to be the same type (both strings or both numeric)
